let __v_206 = Value::from("Two things in a house are called a washer. The ring inside a tap costs pennies: turn the water off at the isolating valve, take the tap apart and take the old ring to a hardware shop to match - half an inch fits most taps, three quarters the older big bath taps. If it is the machine, the fix depends on what it is doing: water on the floor is usually the door seal or a hose, clothes that come out wet is the spin, and no heat is the element. All three are cheap parts, so a machine with a sound drum is worth repairing rather than replacing.");
frame.store("_WASHER_TWO_THINGS", __v_206.clone())?;
let __v_207 = Value::from("Good - then you have what you need. Turn the water off at the isolating valve under the sink or the small screw on the pipe, take the handle off and unscrew the head, then pick the old washer out with a small screwdriver. Match it at a hardware shop: half an inch fits most taps, three quarters the older big bath taps. A smear of silicone grease on the new one and it goes back the same way, and the spanner is for the big nut under the handle.");
frame.store("_THE_TAP_WASHER", __v_207.clone())?;
